entityDescription:
GROW UP is a social agricultural enterprise based in Turin and Pinerolo, established to promote an innovative and replicable model of urban and peri-urban agriculture, blending rural tradition with advanced technologies. As a Third Sector Entity, it integrates sustainable food production, environmental education, social inclusion, and urban regeneration.
It operates through two key locations: Cascina Cassotti Balbo (the first officially recognized Educational Farm in the City of Turin) and Cascina Ainana in Pinerolo, where it develops resilient agricultural practices such as aquaponics, composting, regenerative agriculture, and alpaca farming (Alpaca del Monviso project).
Its activities include:
Accredited Educational Farm for schools, families, and vocational training;

Social Farm and Animal-Assisted Interventions (AAI);

Work inclusion projects for people in vulnerable conditions;

Environmental education and urban climate action projects;

Development of energy communities and local food supply chains.

GROW UP adheres to the Disability Agenda, promotes the One Health approach, and participates in local and European networks in the fields of agroecology, social innovation, and environmental sustainability.
